WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.117 --> 00:00:08.268
AI provenance and reviewer sign-off, on the same scan.

2
00:00:08.268 --> 00:00:15.271
Each file gets an AI-generated estimate — a probability from code signals, not proof of authorship — and a content hash.

3
00:00:15.271 --> 00:00:22.278
A reviewer signs off (simulated here). The sign-off is bound to this exact content hash.

4
00:00:22.278 --> 00:00:29.286
Now the code changes…

5
00:00:29.286 --> 00:00:36.306
…and is scanned again.

6
00:00:36.306 --> 00:00:43.309
The content hash changed, so the old sign-off no longer covers the file: a reviewer must attest again.
